@startuml "Composite - Equipment - Class Diagram"
skinparam nodesep 20
skinparam linetype polyline
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members
title Composite — GoF's equipment example, where the roll-up is money


abstract class Equipment <<Component>> {
  + name() : String
  + power() : int
  + netPrice() : Currency
  + discountPrice() : Currency
}

class FloppyDisk <<Leaf>>
class Card <<Leaf>>
abstract class CompositeEquipment <<Composite>> {
  - parts : List<Equipment>
}
class Chassis
class Cabinet
class Bus

Equipment <|-- FloppyDisk
Equipment <|-- Card
Equipment <|-- CompositeEquipment
CompositeEquipment <|-- Chassis
CompositeEquipment <|-- Cabinet
CompositeEquipment <|-- Bus

note bottom of CompositeEquipment
  netPrice() adds up the parts.
  A cabinet holding a chassis holding
  cards answers one number, and no
  client writes the loop.
end note

CompositeEquipment o-[norank]-> "*" Equipment : parts
CompositeEquipment -[hidden]- Cabinet
Chassis -[hidden]right- Cabinet
Cabinet -[hidden]right- Bus
@enduml
